        ("What is the difference between Object.is() and === for +0 and -0?", "Object.is(+0, -0) evaluates to false. === evaluates +0 === -0 to true.", "Intermediate", "Comparison", "Object.is(+0, -0); // false\n+0 === -0; // true", "Why does Object.is distinguish them?"),
