        ("What does Promise.allSettled() solve that Promise.all() cannot?", "Promise.allSettled waits for all promises to finish even if some reject. Promise.all aborts immediately on the first rejection.", "Easy", "Comparison", "", "What format do settled objects have?"),
        ("What does Promise.any() reject with when all promises fail?", "It rejects with an AggregateError containing all individual rejection reasons in its .errors property.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "", "What is the difference between Promise.any and Promise.race?"),
        ("What is RegExp sticky flag /y in ES6?", "The 'y' flag performs 'sticky' matching: it matches only from the exact position indicated by the lastIndex property of the regular expression.", "Advanced", "Concept", "const regex = /foo/y;", "How does sticky differ from global /g?"),
        ("What is RegExp unicode flag /u in ES6?", "The 'u' flag enables full Unicode handling, treating surrogate pairs as single characters in character sets and dot wildcards.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "/^.$/u.test('👍'); // true", "What happens without the 'u' flag on emoji?"),
        ("What is RegExp dotAll flag /s in ES2018?", "The 's' flag allows the dot (.) wildcard to match newline characters (\\n, \\r), which it normally does not match.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "/hello.world/s.test('hello\\nworld'); // true", "How did developers match all characters before /s?"),
        ("What are RegExp named capture groups in ES2018?", "Groups named with (?<name>...) format whose captured matches can be read via match.groups.name instead of numerical indices.", "Intermediate", "Practical", "const regex = /(?<year>\\d{4})-(?<month>\\d{2})/;\nconst { groups: { year, month } } = regex.exec('2026-10');", "Why are named capture groups clearer?"),
        ("What are RegExp lookbehind assertions in ES2018?", "Positive lookbehind (?<=...) and negative lookbehind (?<!...) assert that what precedes the current match matches or does not match a pattern.", "Advanced", "Concept", "const price = /(?<=\\$)\\d+/.exec('$100')[0]; // '100'", "How does lookbehind differ from lookahead?"),
        ("What does Promise.prototype.finally() do in ES2018?", "finally(callback) executes cleanup logic when a promise settles (fulfilled or rejected) and yields the original promise result unchanged.", "Easy", "Practical", "fetch(url).then(handle).catch(err).finally(cleanup);", "Does finally receive any arguments?"),
